# Copy to .env and fill in as each milestone needs them. All optional until their milestone.

# --- M1: Bluesky analytics fetch (free) ---
# Create an app password at https://bsky.app/settings/app-passwords
BLUESKY_HANDLE=
BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- Substack Notes (free, no key) ---
# Your profile @handle (from substack.com/@<handle>), used by `npm run new-notes` to pull your
# Notes for spreading + analytics. Can differ from your publication subdomain.
SUBSTACK_HANDLE=
# Keyed HMAC secret for account-level research respondent pseudonyms. Required before capture.
RESEARCH_HASH_KEY=

# --- Pattern mining: Reddit API (free, read-only) ---
# Used by `npm run patterns:reddit` to collect subreddit posts WITH their scores, plus an unbiased
# /new window that gives each community a true median to measure winners against. Read-only:
# application-only OAuth, no Reddit account password, nothing is ever posted.
# Create the app: https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> "create another app..." -> type "script",
# redirect uri http://localhost:8080 (unused, but the form requires one).
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID is the short string shown under the app name, below "personal use script".
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Reddit's API rules require a descriptive agent in this exact shape, and reject generic ones:
#   platform:app-id:version (by /u/your-reddit-username)
# REDDIT_USER_AGENT=nodejs:content-agents-patterns:1.0 (by /u/your-username)
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=

# --- Pattern mining: Instagram via Meta Graph API business_discovery (free, read-only) ---
# Used by `npm run patterns:instagram` to read other creators' recent posts: caption, likes,
# comments, permalink, timestamp, media type, and (for Reels ONLY) a public view_count that no
# other route we have exposes. It returns NO transcript, no caption track, no on-screen text and
# no carousel slide text, because no such field exists in the API, so every entry it writes is
# body_is_complete: false. That is honest, not a bug: substance still has to be hand-collected.
#
# Setup, roughly an afternoon. Standard Access is enough because only you use the app, so there is
# no App Review and no Business Verification.
#   1. Instagram app, Settings, Account type and tools: switch to a Business or Creator account.
#   2. Link that account to a Facebook Page you can administer. business_discovery is available
#      only on the Facebook-Login flavour of the API, so the Page is not optional.
#   3. developers.facebook.com/apps: create an app and fill in Basic settings.
#   4. App Dashboard: add the "Facebook Login for Business" product. Defaults are fine.
#   5. developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer: pick the app, generate a User token granting
#      instagram_basic, instagram_manage_insights, pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement.
#   6. GET /me/accounts for the Page id, then GET /<PAGE_ID>?fields=instagram_business_account
#      for your own Instagram user id.
#   7. Explorer tokens last about an hour. Exchange for a roughly 60 day one:
#      GET /oauth/access_token?grant_type=fb_exchange_token&client_id=<APP_ID>
#        &client_secret=<APP_SECRET>&fb_exchange_token=<SHORT_TOKEN>
# Then check every seeded Instagram account with one live query each, before collecting anything:
#   npm run patterns:instagram -- --smoke
# It prints, per account, whether the handle is readable at all (a personal, age-gated or wrong
# handle returns nothing) and which fields came back with a value, came back EMPTY, or never came
# back at all. Those last two are different problems and the report keeps them apart.
#
# Permanently unavailable on this route, so nobody re-investigates them: saved_count, shares_count
# and total_views_count. metrics.shares is therefore null on every entry, never 0.
#
# The long-lived Facebook User access token from step 7. Expires; the collector says so plainly.
IG_GRAPH_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# YOUR OWN Instagram professional account id from step 6, not the account you want to read.
IG_GRAPH_USER_ID=
# Optional. Defaults to v25.0, the version Meta's own Business Discovery examples use.
# IG_GRAPH_API_VERSION=v25.0

# --- Automated analytics pull (constrained browser agent) — see docs/setup-analytics-pull.md ---
# No credentials here by design: run `npm run pull:login -- linkedin` once, log in by hand, and the
# session saves to a per-platform Chrome profile OUTSIDE the repo (~/.content-agents), never committed.
# Optional override for where those profiles live:
# CONTENT_AGENTS_HOME=/absolute/path/to/.content-agents

# --- M4+: image generation + transcription (Gemini) ---
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Voiceover TTS ---
# Default is Kokoro (local + free) — see docs/setup-kokoro.md.
#   server mode: run kokoro-fastapi (Docker) and point KOKORO_URL at it
#   cli mode (lightweight, no Docker): KOKORO_MODE=cli + KOKORO_CMD=scripts/kokoro-tts
#     (Kokoro-ONNX in a local venv — see "Option C" in docs/setup-kokoro.md)
KOKORO_MODE=server
KOKORO_URL=http://localhost:8880/v1/audio/speech
KOKORO_VOICE=af_heart
# cli mode:
# KOKORO_MODE=cli
# KOKORO_CMD=/absolute/path/to/repo/scripts/kokoro-tts
# KOKORO_CMD=kokoro-tts
# Kokoro emits no timestamps → captions come from a Whisper forced-alignment pass:
WHISPER_BACKEND=whispercpp
WHISPER_CPP_BIN=whisper-cli           # whisper.cpp binary on PATH (or absolute path)
WHISPER_CPP_MODEL=models/ggml-base.en.bin
# Fallback TTS — set tts: elevenlabs in config/providers.yaml to use it (~$6/mo, timestamps built in)
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# --- Outreach engine (docs/outreach-engine-plan.md) ---
# Read-only path to job-search-agent's manual_research.db (sibling repo), used by
# `/outreach add --from-jsa` (intake, not built yet) and the Follow-ups tab's jobsearch-bucket
# read (Phase 4). src/outreach/jsa.ts opens it with better-sqlite3 `readonly: true` -- never
# writes, never live-links (snapshot-on-intake per plan §2a).
JSA_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/job-search-agent/manual_research.db

# --- M7: publishing ---
# https://typefully.com/settings/api  (covers X + LinkedIn + Bluesky as scheduled drafts)
TYPEFULLY_API_KEY=
# YouTube OAuth — see docs/setup-youtube-oauth.md
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# TikTok via PostPeer (sanctioned API relay; 20 free posts/mo, then never-expiring credits) — see docs/setup-tiktok.md
POSTPEER_API_KEY=
POSTPEER_TIKTOK_ACCOUNT_ID=            # the connected TikTok account's accountId (list accounts in PostPeer to get it)
# TIKTOK_SCHEDULE_AT=                  # explicit ISO-8601 time to schedule the post; omit to use the lead time below
# TIKTOK_SCHEDULE_LEAD_MIN=60          # with no TIKTOK_SCHEDULE_AT, schedule this many minutes after /publish runs

# Quote-card (image) auto-publishing — native Typefully image posts since 2026-07-08 (reuses
# TYPEFULLY_API_KEY / TYPEFULLY_SOCIAL_SET_ID above; no separate keys needed). PostPeer/Upload-Post
# are retired for cards — POSTPEER_API_KEY above is now used for TikTok only.

# --- OpenRouter (Grok script writer + image-gen bakeoff) ---
# One key powers both: the video-script writer AND every OpenRouter image model in the
# `npm run bakeoff` lineup (config/bakeoff.yaml). https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_GROK_MODEL=x-ai/grok-4
# OPENROUTER_GROK_COST_PER_1K=0.015    # approx output cost per 1k tokens, for the cost log
# Build 2 fiction prose (the /story skill). Same key; separate model/cost/temperature so prose
# can run hotter than the video-script writer. Defaults: grok-4, 0.015/1k, temp 0.9.
# OPENROUTER_PROSE_MODEL=x-ai/grok-4
# OPENROUTER_PROSE_COST_PER_1K=0.015
# OPENROUTER_PROSE_TEMPERATURE=0.9
